.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NVRAM 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvram
.Nd read and set firmware variables
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl f Ar filename
.Op Fl d Ar name
.Op Fl c
.Ar name Ns Op = Ns Ar value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and sets the firmware's variables, through the
.Ql options
entry of the I/O Kit device tree.
Values print with each byte that does not print as
.Ql % Ns Ar xx ,
and may be given the same way.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Delete every variable.
.It Fl d Ar name
Delete
.Ar name .
.It Fl f Ar filename
Set the variables in
.Ar filename ,
one
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
per line.
.It Fl p
Print every variable.
.It Fl x
Print them as an XML property list.
.It Ar name
Print
.Ar name .
.It Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
Set
.Ar name .
.El
.Pp
Setting and deleting need a firmware NVRAM driver; without one, as
Minkar is now, they fail with
.Dq unsupported function .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioreg 8
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
